# Alert module boundaries

`/api/state` imports `daily-tasks-digest` → `free-bet-lots`. If that lots module
imports `@/lib/services/quiet-alerts`, Turbopack compiles quiet-alerts into the
state route. A missing or not-yet-bound named export then fails the **entire
app** with `Export X doesn't exist in target module`.

## Do

- Put dedupe key helpers in `edgeways/src/lib/alerts/expiring-alert-keys.ts`
  (leaf: no db, no `server-only`, no `rules.ts`).
- Import those keys from `quiet-alerts.ts`. Do **not** import `@/lib/alerts/rules`
  from `quiet-alerts.ts`.
- Call `quietOfferAlerts` / `quietFreeBetAlerts` from the **mutation API**
  (`api/accounts/free-bets`, `api/offers/[id]`) or from `offers.ts` status
  transitions. Add a test import of any new `quiet*` export in
  `quiet-alerts.test.ts` in the same change.

## Do not

- Import `@/lib/services/quiet-alerts` from `free-bet-lots.ts`, other
  `src/lib/accounts/*` modules, `daily-tasks-digest.ts`, or `state.ts`.
- Add a `quiet*` function in an importer before it exists on `quiet-alerts.ts`.
